{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>And I will dwell.</b> He tells how the Glory will dwell in the midst of the children of Israel when the standards are set up, for the four standards were at the four sides, and a partition between the camp of Levi and the camp of Israel, for they too were at the four sides and afterward a partition, and the tent there in the midst of the children of Israel. Now one with a discharge did not go out from the camp of Israel, nor did they have permission to dwell outside the boundary; rather, the command applied to the camp of Israel when it went out to war against the enemy. And likewise 'when the camp goes out' (Deuteronomy 23:10) does not speak of the camp of all Israel, men, women, and children, for those who go out to war are males and few. And when they carried the ark with them, as Phinehas did, they could not make a partition for the place of the ark."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:16.377233454Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}